# GhostInTheCodebase — environment variables
# Copy to .env (never commit .env) and adjust per environment.

# ── Demo application (required) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Controls the invoice store's ownership behavior.
#   on  → ownership enforced: cross-owner reads return 403 (the shipped/deployed state)
#   off → the recorded BOLA hole is live (demo narrative only — never deploy this way)
# REQUIRED on Vercel: SECURE_MODE=on
SECURE_MODE=on

# ── Metadata (auto-provided, listed for completeness) ─────────────────────
# Set automatically by Vercel; used only for metadataBase/og-image URLs.
# Locally the code falls back to http://localhost:3000.
# VERCEL_URL=ghostinthecodebase.vercel.app

# ── Not needed yet (Ghost Cloud, MVP 2) ───────────────────────────────────
# When Ghost Cloud lands, these will be added to the local recorder / CLI —
# NOT to this demo app:
#   GHOST_API_URL      - Ghost Cloud session API endpoint
#   GHOST_Device_TOKEN - one-time device pairing token (never a repo secret)
#   DATABASE_URL       - Neon PostgreSQL, lives in Ghost Cloud only
#
# Secrets policy (see README): full source code and tokens/API keys are never
# synced by Ghost; secrets stay on the machine.
